Thus the \(K^{*0}\) yields have to be corrected by the branching ratio \(2/3\) since we measured the \(K^{*0}\) through the channel with two oppositely charged daughters.

The \(K^{*0}\) transverse mass \(m_{T}\) is defined as

\[m_{T}=\sqrt{m_{0}^{2}+p_{T}^{2}} \tag{4.1}\]

in which \(m_{0}\) is the \(K^{*0}\) natural mass 896.1 MeV/c\({}^{2}\) and \(p_{T}\) is the transverse momentum. We can see that

\[p_{T}dp_{T}=\frac{\sqrt{m_{0}^{2}+p_{T}^{2}}}{2\sqrt{m_{0}^{2}+p_{T}^{2}}}dp_{ T}^{2}=m_{T}dm_{T} \tag{4.2}\]

The total reconstruction efficiency and decay branching ratio corrected \((K^{*0}+\overline{K^{*0}})/2\) invariant yield at mid-rapidity is then

\[\frac{1}{2\pi p_{T}}\frac{d^{2}N}{dydp_{T}}=\frac{1}{2\pi m_{T}}\frac{d^{2}N}{ dydm_{T}} \tag{4.3}\]

Table 4.2 lists the \((K^{*0}+\overline{K^{*0}})/2\) invariant yields \([1/(2\pi m_{T})][d^{2}N/dydm_{T}]\) at mid-rapidity in each \(m_{T}-m_{0}\) bin in central Au+Au and p+p collisions.

Table 4.3 lists the \((K^{*0}+\overline{K^{*0}})/2\) invariant yields at mid-rapidity in each \(m_{T}-m_{0}\) bin in 0-10%, 10%-30%, 30%-50% and 50%-80% centralities in minimum bias Au+Au collisions. The \(m_{T}\) for each \(m_{T}-m_{0}\) bin is calculated from Equation 4.1 using the bin center

